--- a/hw/vfb/man/Xvfb.man
+++ b/hw/vfb/man/Xvfb.man
@@ -70,6 +70,12 @@
 This option only exists on machines that have the mmap and msync system
 calls.
 .TP 4
+.B "\-fbfd \fIdescriptor\fP"
+This option puts screen 0's framebuffer, laid out as with \fB\-fbdir\fP,
+in the already open file \fIdescriptor\fP the server inherited (for
+example a memfd its parent also maps), sized by the server. No file is
+created or removed, and nothing is synced. Only screen 0 can have one.
+.TP 4
 .B "\-shmem"
 This option specifies that the framebuffer should be put in shared memory.
 The shared memory ID for each screen will be printed by the server.
